@format 1
@id section-modification.common.keyboard-shortcuts
@title Keyboard shortcuts
@section Section modification
@area Common
@entry window-key,viewer-key
@summary Resolve configurable SectionStart, SectionSplit, and SectionEnd bindings from the main-window or Split-viewer keyboard surfaces before dispatching the existing-section modification commands.
@related section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section, section-modification.split-selected-section, section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag modification
@tag shortcut

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias binding = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LBinding
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[window-key] Main-window PreviewKeyDown <input>
- Forward PreviewKeyDown into the shared shortcut processor @ window.PShortcutKeyHandle(...)
> keyboard-entry

[viewer-key] Split viewer PreviewKeyDown <input>
- Forward the viewer key event through PViewerKeyDispatch and the window viewer-key adapter into the same shortcut processor @ viewer.PViewerKeyHandle(...)
@ window.PShortcutViewerHandle(...)
> keyboard-entry

[keyboard-entry] Keyboard event convergence <junction>
> text-input-check

[text-input-check] Text-entry guard <decision>
- PShortcutKeyProcess ignores input originating inside TextBoxBase or PasswordBox; otherwise it resolves the physical key and modifiers @ window.PShortcutKeyProcess(...)
@ window.PWindowInputFind(...)
? "Text-entry source" > shortcut-ignored
? "Normal shortcut source" > binding-resolve

[shortcut-ignored] Shortcut ignored <output>
= No section modification command is dispatched.

[binding-resolve] Resolve configured binding <decision>
- Format the current gesture and ask LBindingTokenFind for the currently configured command token @ window.PShortcutDispatch(...)
@ binding.LBindingTokenFind(...)
? "SectionStart" > start-token
? "SectionSplit" > split-token
? "SectionEnd" > end-token
? "Any other or unbound token" > unrelated-token

[unrelated-token] Not a boundary-modification shortcut <output>
= This keyboard event is outside the requested section-modification scope.

[start-token] Translate SectionStart <process>
- PShortcutCodeRead converts SectionStart to setStart, then PShortcutRun delegates it to the active flow @ window.PShortcutCodeRead(...)
@ window.PShortcutRun(...)
> start-dispatch

[split-token] Translate SectionSplit <process>
- PShortcutCodeRead converts SectionSplit to splitSection, then PShortcutRun delegates it to the active flow @ window.PShortcutCodeRead(...)
@ window.PShortcutRun(...)
> split-dispatch

[end-token] Translate SectionEnd <process>
- PShortcutCodeRead converts SectionEnd to setEnd, then PShortcutRun delegates it to the active flow @ window.PShortcutCodeRead(...)
@ window.PShortcutRun(...)
> end-dispatch

[start-dispatch] Dispatch setStart <process>
- PFlowShortcutDispatch receives setStart; the linked map follows only its existing-section modification branch @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setStart
> map:section-modification.set-start-on-selected-section

[split-dispatch] Dispatch splitSection <process>
- PFlowShortcutDispatch receives splitSection and enters the existing-section split manipulation @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / splitSection
> map:section-modification.split-selected-section

[end-dispatch] Dispatch setEnd <process>
- PFlowShortcutDispatch receives setEnd; the linked map follows only its existing-section modification branch @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...) / setEnd
> map:section-modification.set-end-on-selected-section
